# RU(a - b), through add_up_1 on a and -b (milestone2.md, "Rounding a sum down and up").
kernel:        sub_up_1
input:         a
input:         b
output:        r
value:         a-b
ensures:       rounded r up
min_precision: 2
source:        add_up_1 on a and -b (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
theorem:       proofs/theories/DirectedSum.v sub_up_1_correct
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeDirected.v sub_up_1_ieee_correct
cone_exempt:   through add_up_1, whose result is selected

nb = neg(b)
r  = add_up_1(a, nb)
